# /opt/mkt/secrets/backup.env (root, 0600). Read by the backup service only (docs/operations.md, "Backups").
# The owner's age public key (age1..., from `age-keygen` on the owner's own machine): every backup is encrypted
# to it. It is not a secret, and the private key is never put on the server. Blank until the owner gives it: the
# backup then refuses to run and says why.
BACKUP_AGE_RECIPIENT=
